thread:
maya: Heads-up — docs PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/7890 sample in /docs/sdk/rust/prefetch.md is failing CI after a runtime rename (kv_prefetch -> prefetch_kv). CI error: `error: no function named kv_prefetch`

devin: I can take the snippet change. Do we want to show the tiny-batch pattern + prefetch example, or keep it minimal?

maya: minimal but correct. show one async example that prefetches keys, awaits, then streams tokens — short and copy-pasteable. also the quant profiles table still references `q4_kv` which we swapped out for `q4_fast_kv` last quarter. need a short migration note.

sam: I pushed a branch with a quick replacement, but streaming example tests are failing locally. link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/compare/fix/rust-prefetch-snippet

cheng: paste the failing snippet here and I can run it in a container.

sam: Old snippet (failing):
```rust
// old: uses kv_prefetch, fails after rename
let cache_keys = vec!["k1".into(), "k2".into()];
client.kv_prefetch(cache_keys).await?;
let resp = client.generate_stream(&req).await?;
// ...
```

sam: Proposed fix:
```rust
// new: use prefetch_kv and short-batch pattern
let cache_keys = vec!["k1".into(), "k2".into()];
client.prefetch_kv(cache_keys).await?;
// prefer tiny batches for short sequences to hit low-latency path
let resp = client.generate_stream(&req).await?;
// consume stream as usual
```

cheng: ran it locally, the rename patch fixes the compile error. failing test was due to example using a blocking sleep in async context — changed to `tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(10)).await;` and tests pass.

docs-bot: PR #7890 CI: rust-docs-lint failed (sample formatting), code-sample-test failed (streaming smoke).

olivia: I'll update the quant profiles table and add a migration footnote: `runtime v1.4.0: function rename kv_prefetch -> prefetch_kv; q4_kv replaced by q4_fast_kv; for short sequences (<64 tokens) prefer q2_kv for better perf/cost tradeoff.`

devin: also add a one-liner in CHANGELOG.md under /docs/release-notes: "Migration: kv_prefetch renamed to prefetch_kv; update SDK snippets." I can add a small test that runs the rust sample through the sample-runner.

maya: plan: @devin add test + PR update for sample formatting, @olivia update table + migration footnote, @sam rebase your branch and include the `tokio::time::sleep` fix, then I'll re-run CI and merge after green. sound good? :+1:

sam: on it — will rebase and push in ~30m.

devin: will open a tiny PR with test and changelog entry.

olivia: updating table now, will ping when done.

maya: thanks all. I'll do a final pass on wording (short, clear migration notes only).

cheng: lgtm from my side, nice catch on the sleep.

docs-bot: automated note: please add `@docs-bot sample-run` in the PR body to trigger sample-runner once updates are pushed.

maya: added to PR description. merging plan once CI is green. :rocket:
